{"work_id":"parasakthi","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"scene_status":"review","unit_count":39,"units":[{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u001","kind":"stage-direction","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/scenes/scene-20.md","source_locator":{"kind":"scene-parenthetical-block","ordinal":1,"description":"Compressed location marker: road."},"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The verified source has the compressed form `இடம்ரோடு`, read as a location marker rather than silently altering the Tamil."],"english_text":"(Location: road.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u002","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d001","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Vadai! Murukku! Sir! Do you want murukku?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u003","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d002","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Give me three annas' worth."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u004","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d003","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["`போணி` is the trader's first/auspicious sale; it is rendered contextually as `first sale` rather than retained as unexplained jargon."],"english_text":"Good God! It's been three days since I've made a first sale. How much vadai and how much murukku?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u005","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d004","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The source embeds `(கொடுக்கிறான்)` inside Gunasekaran's record; context makes the vendor the giver, but the Tamil record itself remains unchanged."],"english_text":"Give me this for two annas and that for one anna, man! (The vendor gives it.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u006","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d005","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Your hand works all right, doesn't it?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u007","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d006","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":24,"printed_page":23}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The English preserves the source pun on `நடக்கு`, which can mean both `work/function` and `walk`."],"english_text":"A hand doesn't walk—the leg walks. (He shows this with a gesture.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u008","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d007","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Ayyo—poor thing, you seem very hungry. Eat, eat!"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u009","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d008","speaker_label":"அடுத்த","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Hey... murukku."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u010","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d009","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Wait, I'll get the money from this gentleman. Take out the money, man—mm—take it out—"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u011","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d010","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"(He laughs.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u012","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d011","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Why are you laughing, man?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u013","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d012","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"(He laughs again.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u014","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d013","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Hey! Why are you laughing again? Take out the money; I have four streets to cover."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u015","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d014","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The reply plays on `எடு` in `காசை எடு` (`take out the money`) versus the physical sense `pick up`; the English keeps the joke approximately without adding a new action."],"english_text":"Why—pick what up?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u016","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d015","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Who is this insolent fellow? I said take out the money."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u017","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d016","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Hey!—Money? For you? What for?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u018","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d017","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["`மாமா மச்சான் மாதிரி` invokes familiar kinship terms; the English retains the source relation pair rather than replacing it with a generic `friends`."],"english_text":"Why are you fooling around as though we're uncle and brother-in-law? Are you trying to cheat me? Who do you think I am!"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u019","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d018","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Then give me another two annas' worth."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u020","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d019","speaker_label":"வியா","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Now you're talking! Here, take it. (He gives it; Gunasekaran eats.) Take out the money—mm—it's getting late."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u021","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d020","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"(Like a madman.) Ah, you fellow—"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u022","kind":"stage-direction","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/scenes/scene-20.md","source_locator":{"kind":"scene-parenthetical-block","ordinal":2,"description":"Gunasekaran drives the vendor away, lifts the box himself and leaves with it."},"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"(He drives the vendor away, picks up the box himself and sets off.)"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u023","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d021","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Boss, do you want murukku?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u024","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d022","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Is it hot?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u025","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d023","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Both are."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u026","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d024","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Then give me one anna's worth of this and one anna's worth of that."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u027","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d025","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Take out the money."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u028","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d026","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Hey, give it first."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u029","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d027","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Sir, will two annas' worth be enough for you?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u030","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d028","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["`ஓசி` is rendered as `extra for free`, preserving the bargaining sense rather than translating it as a named item."],"english_text":"Not enough! One shouldn't spend too much money. Since I'm buying for two annas, give me a little extra for free."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u031","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d029","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Ayyo, even here you haven't lost your beggar's mentality! Here, have this free. (He breaks off a little and gives it.) Take out the money."}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u032","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d030","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Money? Do you have change for a rupee?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u033","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d031","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":25,"printed_page":24}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"What?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u034","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d032","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Do you have change for one rupee?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u035","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d033","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The source shifts abruptly from taking the rupee to the mock question `ஏதுங்காணும் இந்தக் காசு?`; the English preserves that comic discontinuity rather than rationalizing the trick."],"english_text":"Change? From me? You fool, hand it here. (He takes the rupee and holds it in his hand.) What a chance—would I let this slip? What is this money, sir?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u036","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d034","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"What, sir—this money?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u037","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d035","speaker_label":"குண","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The source code-switch `எய்ட் நாட்திரீ` is rendered phonetically as `eight nought three`.","The verified source word `கொட்டாபுளி` is semantically unclear in this context and is retained transparently as `kottapuli` rather than assigned an unsupported insult or object."],"english_text":"Hey, 'eight nought three'—take this kottapuli away! [He runs off with the rupee.]"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u038","kind":"dialogue","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/dialogues/records/scene-20.json","source_record_id":"parasakthi-s020-d036","speaker_label":"முத","page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":[],"english_text":"Fine—the box is still here, isn't it?"}},{"id":"parasakthi-en-s020-u039","kind":"stage-direction","status":"review","target_language":"en","canonical_scene":20,"source":{"source_path":"works/parasakthi/scenes/scene-20.md","source_locator":{"kind":"scene-bracketed-stage-block","ordinal":1,"description":"The vendor returns for the box; the proprietor resists; the box is put on his head and police make an arrest."},"page_provenance":[{"pdf_page":26,"printed_page":25}]},"translation":{"mode":"prose-faithful","notes":["The final source `பிடித்துக்கொண்டு போதல்` does not explicitly name which man the police take. The English retains the source's pronoun-level ambiguity rather than specifying an arrested person."],"english_text":"[The vendor comes and lifts the box... The proprietor refuses to let him take it. The vendor lifts the box and puts it on the proprietor's head; at once the police arrive, seize him and take him away.]"}}]}